 as a  twitter account to just to  see what kind of level of interest there  was just to see if people still cared  about american made yeah and they did it  there was instant  interest and that grew into the site the  links to the products go along with some  advice too what would you tell folks out  there in the market for this gift giving  season i would encourage shoppers to  remember the businesses that were there  for them  during these last couple of difficult  years it's really up to the consumer  every single one product that i buy  makes a difference to a business  and makes a difference to a worker whose  job  is part of that business  and this trend of  u.s companies sending jobs overseas  began in 1980 we lost 7.5  million u.s manufacturing jobs in the  last 30 years it is just incredible to  see the possibility the possibility of  it coming back great ingenuity sign me  up for socks from fort payne  sock capital of the world

